⚙️ Installation & Setup
Clone the Repository

Bash
git clone [https://github.com/faizal-khan-a/CKD-Prediction-Web-App.git](https://github.com/faizal-khan-a/CKD-Prediction-Web-App.git)
Navigate to the Project

Bash
cd CKD-Prediction-Web-App
Create a Virtual Environment

Bash
python -m venv venv
Activate the Virtual Environment

Windows PowerShell:

PowerShell
venv\Scripts\activate
If you receive an execution policy error:

PowerShell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
venv\Scripts\activate
Install Dependencies

Bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
▶️ How to Run the Application
After installing the dependencies, run:

Bash
python app.py
The Flask application will start locally. Open your browser and visit:

Plaintext
[http://127.0.0.1:5000](http://127.0.0.1:5000)
🔬 How the Application Works
User Registration: The user creates an account through the Sign Up page.

Sign In: The user signs into the application.

Patient Data Entry: The user enters the required clinical parameters.

Data Preparation: The Flask application prepares the entered values according to the Machine Learning model's expected feature structure.

Model Prediction: The saved model.pkl file is loaded and used to generate the prediction.

Display Result: The prediction result is displayed to the user.

Store Patient Record: The patient information can be stored in the SQLite database.

Generate PDF: A patient report can be generated in PDF format.

📌 Key Project Highlights
End-to-end Machine Learning web application

Flask-based backend architecture

Scikit-learn Machine Learning model serialized using Joblib

SQLite database integration with SQLAlchemy ORM, Flask-Migrate, and Alembic

User registration and authentication workflows

Clinical parameter input form and prediction pipeline

Patient record management and PDF report generation

